{
 "_about": "What a common test is made of — names, a group, and the unit most laboratories print — offered on a test's page when it has no components yet (utils/lab_parts). Structure only: there is not one figure in this file, and there must never be one. Ranges and critical limits are the laboratory's own, from its analyser's kit insert, and arrive by import, by hand or from the insert reader, approved by its director. A unit here is a suggestion the laboratory can change before saving. Specimen-specific names (Urine Glucose, Stool Pus Cells) are kept apart from the blood ones because a range belongs to an analyte, and urine glucose is not blood glucose.",
